# No dashes in copy

Never use em dashes (—) or en dashes (–) in user-facing text for this project.

Includes: homepage copy, guides (`content/guides/`), UI strings, meta descriptions, button labels, and any text visitors or readers see.

## Use instead

| Instead of | Use |
|------------|-----|
| `thing — other thing` | `thing. other thing` or `thing, other thing` |
| `step 1 — do this` | `step 1: do this` or `step 1. do this` |
| `buy it — it's worth it` | `buy it. it's worth it` |

## Still allowed

- Hyphens in compound words: `step-by-step`, `copy-paste`, `real-time`
- Hyphens in code, URLs, file paths, CSS, and technical identifiers
- Minus signs in math or numbers

## When editing existing content

If you find em or en dashes in user-facing copy, replace them as part of the change. Do not introduce new ones.
